courses.learning_outcomes:
1. Recognize how different aspects of life sciences make various impacts on the society and environment of Hong Kong;
2. Design a group research project to address the scientific questions or problems related to the society and environment of Hong Kong;
3. Read scientific literature relevant to their research project;
4. Acquire practical research skills of information search from various types of databases and/or hands-on research techniques in conducting experiments;
5. Recognize, analyze, and comment on the scientific and ethical issues of certain basic research and applications of different fields of life sciences in Hong Kong;
6. Develop practical skills in team building, problem-solving and communication through different types of learning activities;
7. Develop a sense of responsibility and team spirit;
8. Improve skills in writing scientific proposal;
9. Gain learning methodologies that promote life-long learning in life sciences to promote its impact on the society.

1. 認識生命科學的不同方面如何對香港的社會和環境產生各種影響；
2. 設計小組研究計劃，以解決與香港社會和環境有關的科學問題；
3. 閱讀與其研究項目有關的科學文獻；
4. 從各種類型的數據庫中獲得信息搜索的實踐研究技能和/或進行實驗的研究技術；
5. 認識，分析和評論香港生命科學各個領域的某些基礎研究和應用的科學和倫理問題；
6. 通過不同類型的學習活動，培養團隊建設，解決問題和交流方面的實踐技能；
7. 培養責任心和團隊合作精神；
8. 提高科學寫作和口頭表達能力；
9. 獲得終身學習生命科學知識的學習方法並促進其對社會的影響。
